# Vendored MAFFT. The official all-in-one packages ship a shell driver
# (mafft.bat) whose line endings must stay LF: upstream's Windows page says
# "Make sure to keep LF". Git's end-of-line conversion would rewrite it to CRLF
# on a Windows checkout and break the driver, and would corrupt the helper
# executables outright. Treat the whole vendored tree as binary so nothing in
# it is ever normalised.
app/packaging/vendor/mafft/** -text
